style='font-size:12.0pt'>          As part of our standard response to the
gospel, God appointed baptism for expressing personal identification with Jesus
Christ, which involves commitment to his lordship, values, and purposes. In
consequence of our identity with him, God forgives our sin, grants fellowship
with his Spirit, and numbers us among his children.&lt;/span>&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>ABSTRACT OF DISTINCTIONS ABOUT THE NECESSITY OF BAPTISM</title><link>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/baptism/abstract-of-distinctions-about-the-necessity-of-baptism/</link><pubDate>Thu, 02 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://christir.org/essays/topics/christian-doctrine/baptism/abstract-of-distinctions-about-the-necessity-of-baptism/</guid><description>&lt;style>
